# implements-port slice 13 (B3, the root; steps/implements-port-plan.md): at the walked root a value
# of one named primitive type given to a place of another calls the conversion row's receiver on
# it, as in a method (Q33): a call node of the receiver over the value, its result the place's
# value (l2_rw_convert, from l2_rw_texpr).  Here: an int own stored into a size_t own, an int own
# given to a size_t formal of a root call, and a size_t own given to the int field exit_code of the
# exit letter.  Every value fits, so the entry is 7.  The refusal is unit_s13_root_conv_range /
# _catch; a value only the walker types is unit_s13_root_conv_compound.
fn: take (size_t: n) int
    if: n = 5U
        return: 2
    return: 0
end: take
size_t: s 0U
int: x 5
int: t 0
size_t: code 5U
s: x
t: take(x)
if: s = 5U && t = 2
    code: 7U
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: code; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
